      "widgets_values": [
        "{\"version\":1,\"content\":\"<h1>HOW TO USE</h1><p>\\n\\n</p><p>Puts your logo in the bottom right corner of every picture in a folder, in one Run. The Math nodes work out the corner from each picture's own size, so pictures of different sizes all get the logo in the same place. For text instead of a logo, use <b>3. Watermark All Images in a Folder</b>.</p><p>\\n\\n</p><hr class=\\\"pix-note-hr-solid\\\" style=\\\"color: #b8b8b8\\\"><p>\\n\\n</p><h2><span data-ic=\\\"folder-v1\\\" class=\\\"pix-note-ic\\\" contenteditable=\\\"false\\\" style=\\\"color: #f66744\\\"></span>&nbsp;Pick your folder</h2><p>\\n\\n</p><ol><li>On <b>Load Images from Folder Pixaroma</b>, click <b>Browse</b> and pick your folder, or paste the folder's path into the box.</li><li>Click <b>Pick images</b>, then <b>Select all</b>, or click only the pictures you want. The button shows how many are picked.</li><li>Press <b>Run</b> once. Leave the Run count at <b>1</b>: the node sends every picture through by itself, one after the other.</li></ol><p>\\n\\n</p><p>This workflow opens with <b>no folder picked</b>: choose your own folder, or try it first on the demo folder <b>Products</b> inside the <b>Media Inputs</b> folder that comes with these workflows.</p><p>\\n\\n</p><p><span data-ic=\\\"idea\\\" class=\\\"pix-note-ic\\\" contenteditable=\\\"false\\\" style=\\\"color: #f66744\\\"></span>&nbsp;A folder inside ComfyUI's own <code>input</code> or <code>output</code> folder works straight away. A folder anywhere else works too, but pick it once with <b>Browse</b>: that is how ComfyUI knows you allowed it.</p><p>\\n\\n</p><p><span data-ic=\\\"idea\\\" class=\\\"pix-note-ic\\\" contenteditable=\\\"false\\\" style=\\\"color: #f66744\\\"></span>&nbsp;Pictures go through in name order. Name them <code>01_</code>, <code>02_</code> and so on if the order matters.</p><p>\\n\\n</p><hr class=\\\"pix-note-hr-solid\\\" style=\\\"color: #b8b8b8\\\"><p>\\n\\n</p><h2><span data-ic=\\\"image\\\" class=\\\"pix-note-ic\\\" contenteditable=\\\"false\\\" style=\\\"color: #f66744\\\"></span>&nbsp;Your logo</h2><p>\\n\\n</p><ol><li>Click the picture on <b>2. your logo</b> to upload your own logo. A PNG with a see-through background looks best. The demo uses the Pixaroma logo <b>Logo.png</b> from the Media Inputs folder.</li><li>Bigger or smaller: open the gear on that node and change <b>Longest side</b> (160 px in the demo).</li><li>Closer to or further from the edge: change <b>3. distance from the edge</b>.</li></ol><p>\\n\\n</p><hr class=\\\"pix-note-hr-solid\\\" style=\\\"color: #b8b8b8\\\"><p>\\n\\n</p><h2><span data-ic=\\\"chip\\\" class=\\\"pix-note-ic\\\" contenteditable=\\\"false\\\" style=\\\"color: #f66744\\\"></span>&nbsp;Another corner</h2><p>\\n\\n</p><p>Change the two formulas. <b>a</b> = the picture's size, <b>b</b> = the logo's size, <b>c</b> = the distance from the edge:</p><p>\\n\\n</p><table class=\\\"pix-note-grid\\\" style=\\\"--pix-note-grid-border: #f66744; --pix-note-grid-header-bg: #1a1a1a\\\"><thead><tr><th>Corner</th><th>x formula</th><th>y formula</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Bottom right (the demo)</td><td><code>a - b - c</code></td><td><code>a - b - c</code></td></tr><tr><td>Bottom left</td><td><code>c</code></td><td><code>a - b - c</code></td></tr><tr><td>Top right</td><td><code>a - b - c</code></td><td><code>c</code></td></tr><tr><td>Top left</td><td><code>c</code></td><td><code>c</code></td></tr><tr><td>Centre</td><td><code>(a - b) / 2</code></td><td><code>(a - b) / 2</code></td></tr></tbody></table><p>\\n\\n</p><p><span data-ic=\\\"idea\\\" class=\\\"pix-note-ic\\\" contenteditable=\\\"false\\\" style=\\\"color: #f66744\\\"></span>&nbsp;A softer logo: make your PNG half see-through in your picture editor before you load it.</p><p>\\n\\n</p><hr class=\\\"pix-note-hr-solid\\\" style=\\\"color: #b8b8b8\\\"><p>\\n\\n</p><h2><span data-ic=\\\"question-mark\\\" class=\\\"pix-note-ic\\\" contenteditable=\\\"false\\\" style=\\\"color: #f66744\\\"></span>&nbsp;Something not working?</h2><p>\\n\\n</p><p>Each button opens the answer on the Pixaroma help page.</p><p>\\n\\n</p><p><span class=\\\"pix-note-btnblock\\\"><a class=\\\"pix-note-rm\\\" style=\\\"background-color: #f66744\\\" href=\\\"https://workflows.pixaroma.com/help/faq/#q-folder-not-approved\\\" target=\\\"_blank\\\" rel=\\\"noopener noreferrer\\\">Folder not approved</a></span>&nbsp;<span class=\\\"pix-note-btnblock\\\"><a class=\\\"pix-note-rm\\\" style=\\\"background-color: #f66744\\\" href=\\\"https://workflows.pixaroma.com/help/faq/#q-save-other-folder\\\" target=\\\"_blank\\\" rel=\\\"noopener noreferrer\\\">Save to your own folder</a></span>&nbsp;<span class=\\\"pix-note-btnblock\\\"><a class=\\\"pix-note-rm\\\" style=\\\"background-color: #f66744\\\" href=\\\"https://workflows.pixaroma.com/help/look/\\\" target=\\\"_blank\\\" rel=\\\"noopener noreferrer\\\">Nodes look different from the video</a></span>&nbsp;</p><p>\\n\\n</p>\",\"buttonColor\":\"#f66744\",\"lineColor\":\"#f66744\",\"backgroundColor\":\"#2a2a2a\",\"info\":{\"title\":\"How to Use\",\"icon\":\"to-do\",\"color\":\"#2a9d8f\"}}"
      ],
      "widgets_values_named": {
        "note_json": "{\"version\":1,\"content\":\"<h1>HOW TO USE</h1><p>\\n\\n</p><p>Puts your logo in the bottom right corner of every picture in a folder, in one Run. The Math nodes work out the corner from each picture's own size, so pictures of different sizes all get the logo in the same place. For text instead of a logo, use <b>3. Watermark All Images in a Folder</b>.</p><p>\\n\\n</p><hr class=\\\"pix-note-hr-solid\\\" style=\\\"color: #b8b8b8\\\"><p>\\n\\n</p><h2><span data-ic=\\\"folder-v1\\\" class=\\\"pix-note-ic\\\" contenteditable=\\\"false\\\" style=\\\"color: #f66744\\\"></span>&nbsp;Pick your folder</h2><p>\\n\\n</p><ol><li>On <b>Load Images from Folder Pixaroma</b>, click <b>Browse</b> and pick your folder, or paste the folder's path into the box.</li><li>Click <b>Pick images</b>, then <b>Select all</b>, or click only the pictures you want. The button shows how many are picked.</li><li>Press <b>Run</b> once. Leave the Run count at <b>1</b>: the node sends every picture through by itself, one after the other.</li></ol><p>\\n\\n</p><p>This workflow opens with <b>no folder picked</b>: choose your own folder, or try it first on the demo folder <b>Products</b> inside the <b>Media Inputs</b> folder that comes with these workflows.</p><p>\\n\\n</p><p><span data-ic=\\\"idea\\\" class=\\\"pix-note-ic\\\" contenteditable=\\\"false\\\" style=\\\"color: #f66744\\\"></span>&nbsp;A folder inside ComfyUI's own <code>input</code> or <code>output</code> folder works straight away. A folder anywhere else works too, but pick it once with <b>Browse</b>: that is how ComfyUI knows you allowed it.</p><p>\\n\\n</p><p><span data-ic=\\\"idea\\\" class=\\\"pix-note-ic\\\" contenteditable=\\\"false\\\" style=\\\"color: #f66744\\\"></span>&nbsp;Pictures go through in name order. Name them <code>01_</code>, <code>02_</code> and so on if the order matters.</p><p>\\n\\n</p><hr class=\\\"pix-note-hr-solid\\\" style=\\\"color: #b8b8b8\\\"><p>\\n\\n</p><h2><span data-ic=\\\"image\\\" class=\\\"pix-note-ic\\\" contenteditable=\\\"false\\\" style=\\\"color: #f66744\\\"></span>&nbsp;Your logo</h2><p>\\n\\n</p><ol><li>Click the picture on <b>2. your logo</b> to upload your own logo. A PNG with a see-through background looks best. The demo uses the Pixaroma logo <b>Logo.png</b> from the Media Inputs folder.</li><li>Bigger or smaller: open the gear on that node and change <b>Longest side</b> (160 px in the demo).</li><li>Closer to or further from the edge: change <b>3. distance from the edge</b>.</li></ol><p>\\n\\n</p><hr class=\\\"pix-note-hr-solid\\\" style=\\\"color: #b8b8b8\\\"><p>\\n\\n</p><h2><span data-ic=\\\"chip\\\" class=\\\"pix-note-ic\\\" contenteditable=\\\"false\\\" style=\\\"color: #f66744\\\"></span>&nbsp;Another corner</h2><p>\\n\\n</p><p>Change the two formulas. <b>a</b> = the picture's size, <b>b</b> = the logo's size, <b>c</b> = the distance from the edge:</p><p>\\n\\n</p><table class=\\\"pix-note-grid\\\" style=\\\"--pix-note-grid-border: #f66744; --pix-note-grid-header-bg: #1a1a1a\\\"><thead><tr><th>Corner</th><th>x formula</th><th>y formula</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Bottom right (the demo)</td><td><code>a - b - c</code></td><td><code>a - b - c</code></td></tr><tr><td>Bottom left</td><td><code>c</code></td><td><code>a - b - c</code></td></tr><tr><td>Top right</td><td><code>a - b - c</code></td><td><code>c</code></td></tr><tr><td>Top left</td><td><code>c</code></td><td><code>c</code></td></tr><tr><td>Centre</td><td><code>(a - b) / 2</code></td><td><code>(a - b) / 2</code></td></tr></tbody></table><p>\\n\\n</p><p><span data-ic=\\\"idea\\\" class=\\\"pix-note-ic\\\" contenteditable=\\\"false\\\" style=\\\"color: #f66744\\\"></span>&nbsp;A softer logo: make your PNG half see-through in your picture editor before you load it.</p><p>\\n\\n</p><hr class=\\\"pix-note-hr-solid\\\" style=\\\"color: #b8b8b8\\\"><p>\\n\\n</p><h2><span data-ic=\\\"question-mark\\\" class=\\\"pix-note-ic\\\" contenteditable=\\\"false\\\" style=\\\"color: #f66744\\\"></span>&nbsp;Something not working?</h2><p>\\n\\n</p><p>Each button opens the answer on the Pixaroma help page.</p><p>\\n\\n</p><p><span class=\\\"pix-note-btnblock\\\"><a class=\\\"pix-note-rm\\\" style=\\\"background-color: #f66744\\\" href=\\\"https://workflows.pixaroma.com/help/faq/#q-folder-not-approved\\\" target=\\\"_blank\\\" rel=\\\"noopener noreferrer\\\">Folder not approved</a></span>&nbsp;<span class=\\\"pix-note-btnblock\\\"><a class=\\\"pix-note-rm\\\" style=\\\"background-color: #f66744\\\" href=\\\"https://workflows.pixaroma.com/help/faq/#q-save-other-folder\\\" target=\\\"_blank\\\" rel=\\\"noopener noreferrer\\\">Save to your own folder</a></span>&nbsp;<span class=\\\"pix-note-btnblock\\\"><a class=\\\"pix-note-rm\\\" style=\\\"background-color: #f66744\\\" href=\\\"https://workflows.pixaroma.com/help/look/\\\" target=\\\"_blank\\\" rel=\\\"noopener noreferrer\\\">Nodes look different from the video</a></span>&nbsp;</p><p>\\n\\n</p>\",\"buttonColor\":\"#f66744\",\"lineColor\":\"#f66744\",\"backgroundColor\":\"#2a2a2a\",\"info\":{\"title\":\"How to Use\",\"icon\":\"to-do\",\"color\":\"#2a9d8f\"}}"
