      "widgets_values": [
        "{\"version\":1,\"content\":\"<h1>WHAT EACH NODE DOES</h1><p>\\n\\n</p><p>The colour of a node tells you what kind of node it is. Nothing here needs changing except the blue ones.</p><p>\\n\\n</p><hr class=\\\"pix-note-hr-solid\\\" style=\\\"color: #b8b8b8\\\"><p>\\n\\n</p><h2><span data-ic=\\\"chip\\\" class=\\\"pix-note-ic\\\" contenteditable=\\\"false\\\" style=\\\"color: #f66744\\\"></span>&nbsp;The steps you set</h2><p>\\n\\n</p><p>Blue, and numbered. These are the only nodes you need to touch.</p><p>\\n\\n</p><ul><li><b>Load Images from Folder Pixaroma (1. your folder)</b> - Point it at a folder and pick the pictures. Press Run once and every picture gets the logo, one after the other. Its resize is Off, so each picture keeps its own size. Its <b>width</b> and <b>height</b> go to the Math nodes.</li><li><b>Load Image Mini Pixaroma (2. your logo, PNG)</b> - Your logo, best as a PNG with a see-through background. Its gear is set to <b>Longest side 160</b>: the logo's longer side becomes 160 px. Change that number in the gear for a bigger or smaller logo.</li><li><b>Number Pixaroma (3. distance from the edge, px)</b> - How far the logo sits from the right and bottom edges, in pixels.</li></ul><p>\\n\\n</p><hr class=\\\"pix-note-hr-solid\\\" style=\\\"color: #b8b8b8\\\"><p>\\n\\n</p><h2><span data-ic=\\\"chip\\\" class=\\\"pix-note-ic\\\" contenteditable=\\\"false\\\" style=\\\"color: #f66744\\\"></span>&nbsp;The helpers</h2><p>\\n\\n</p><p>Purple. They run by themselves and do the small jobs: count, pick, join or pass things along.</p><p>\\n\\n</p><ul><li><b>Image Info Pixaroma (the logo's size and see-through parts)</b> - Reads the logo's finished <b>width</b> and <b>height</b> and its <b>mask</b>: which parts of the PNG are see-through.</li><li><b>InvertMask (show the logo, hide its background)</b> - Turns the mask around, so the logo itself shows and its see-through background does not. Without it you would paste the empty background instead of the logo.</li><li><b>Math Expression (x = picture width - logo width - edge)</b> - Works out where the logo starts from the left: <code>a - b - c</code> = the picture's width - the logo's width - the distance from the edge. It runs once PER picture, so a bigger picture still gets the logo in its corner.</li><li><b>Math Expression (y = picture height - logo height - edge)</b> - The same from the top: the picture's height - the logo's height - the distance from the edge.</li></ul><p>\\n\\n</p><hr class=\\\"pix-note-hr-solid\\\" style=\\\"color: #b8b8b8\\\"><p>\\n\\n</p><h2><span data-ic=\\\"chip\\\" class=\\\"pix-note-ic\\\" contenteditable=\\\"false\\\" style=\\\"color: #f66744\\\"></span>&nbsp;The work</h2><p>\\n\\n</p><p>Green. They run by themselves.</p><p>\\n\\n</p><ul><li><b>Image Composite Masked (puts the logo on the picture)</b> - Pastes the logo onto the picture at <b>x</b> and <b>y</b>, using the mask so only the logo shows. <b>resize_source</b> stays off: on, it would stretch the logo over the whole picture.</li></ul><p>\\n\\n</p><hr class=\\\"pix-note-hr-solid\\\" style=\\\"color: #b8b8b8\\\"><p>\\n\\n</p><h2><span data-ic=\\\"checkmark\\\" class=\\\"pix-note-ic\\\" contenteditable=\\\"false\\\" style=\\\"color: #f66744\\\"></span>&nbsp;The result</h2><p>\\n\\n</p><p>Dark red, at the end.</p><p>\\n\\n</p><ul><li><b>Save Image Pixaroma (keeps each picture's name)</b> - Saves each picture as JPG into <code>ComfyUI/output/With Logo</code>, named like its picture with <code>_logo</code> at the end.</li></ul><p>\\n\\n</p><hr class=\\\"pix-note-hr-solid\\\" style=\\\"color: #b8b8b8\\\"><p>\\n\\n</p><h2><span data-ic=\\\"info\\\" class=\\\"pix-note-ic\\\" contenteditable=\\\"false\\\" style=\\\"color: #f66744\\\"></span>&nbsp;Readouts</h2><p>\\n\\n</p><p>Dark. Nothing to set: they show you what happened.</p><p>\\n\\n</p><ul><li><b>Run Timer</b> - The dark clock above the result shows how long the last Run took.</li></ul><p>\\n\\n</p>\",\"buttonColor\":\"#f66744\",\"lineColor\":\"#f66744\",\"backgroundColor\":\"#2a2a2a\",\"info\":{\"title\":\"Nodes Info\",\"icon\":\"node-v5\",\"color\":\"#3d7cc9\"}}"
      ],
      "widgets_values_named": {
        "note_json": "{\"version\":1,\"content\":\"<h1>WHAT EACH NODE DOES</h1><p>\\n\\n</p><p>The colour of a node tells you what kind of node it is. Nothing here needs changing except the blue ones.</p><p>\\n\\n</p><hr class=\\\"pix-note-hr-solid\\\" style=\\\"color: #b8b8b8\\\"><p>\\n\\n</p><h2><span data-ic=\\\"chip\\\" class=\\\"pix-note-ic\\\" contenteditable=\\\"false\\\" style=\\\"color: #f66744\\\"></span>&nbsp;The steps you set</h2><p>\\n\\n</p><p>Blue, and numbered. These are the only nodes you need to touch.</p><p>\\n\\n</p><ul><li><b>Load Images from Folder Pixaroma (1. your folder)</b> - Point it at a folder and pick the pictures. Press Run once and every picture gets the logo, one after the other. Its resize is Off, so each picture keeps its own size. Its <b>width</b> and <b>height</b> go to the Math nodes.</li><li><b>Load Image Mini Pixaroma (2. your logo, PNG)</b> - Your logo, best as a PNG with a see-through background. Its gear is set to <b>Longest side 160</b>: the logo's longer side becomes 160 px. Change that number in the gear for a bigger or smaller logo.</li><li><b>Number Pixaroma (3. distance from the edge, px)</b> - How far the logo sits from the right and bottom edges, in pixels.</li></ul><p>\\n\\n</p><hr class=\\\"pix-note-hr-solid\\\" style=\\\"color: #b8b8b8\\\"><p>\\n\\n</p><h2><span data-ic=\\\"chip\\\" class=\\\"pix-note-ic\\\" contenteditable=\\\"false\\\" style=\\\"color: #f66744\\\"></span>&nbsp;The helpers</h2><p>\\n\\n</p><p>Purple. They run by themselves and do the small jobs: count, pick, join or pass things along.</p><p>\\n\\n</p><ul><li><b>Image Info Pixaroma (the logo's size and see-through parts)</b> - Reads the logo's finished <b>width</b> and <b>height</b> and its <b>mask</b>: which parts of the PNG are see-through.</li><li><b>InvertMask (show the logo, hide its background)</b> - Turns the mask around, so the logo itself shows and its see-through background does not. Without it you would paste the empty background instead of the logo.</li><li><b>Math Expression (x = picture width - logo width - edge)</b> - Works out where the logo starts from the left: <code>a - b - c</code> = the picture's width - the logo's width - the distance from the edge. It runs once PER picture, so a bigger picture still gets the logo in its corner.</li><li><b>Math Expression (y = picture height - logo height - edge)</b> - The same from the top: the picture's height - the logo's height - the distance from the edge.</li></ul><p>\\n\\n</p><hr class=\\\"pix-note-hr-solid\\\" style=\\\"color: #b8b8b8\\\"><p>\\n\\n</p><h2><span data-ic=\\\"chip\\\" class=\\\"pix-note-ic\\\" contenteditable=\\\"false\\\" style=\\\"color: #f66744\\\"></span>&nbsp;The work</h2><p>\\n\\n</p><p>Green. They run by themselves.</p><p>\\n\\n</p><ul><li><b>Image Composite Masked (puts the logo on the picture)</b> - Pastes the logo onto the picture at <b>x</b> and <b>y</b>, using the mask so only the logo shows. <b>resize_source</b> stays off: on, it would stretch the logo over the whole picture.</li></ul><p>\\n\\n</p><hr class=\\\"pix-note-hr-solid\\\" style=\\\"color: #b8b8b8\\\"><p>\\n\\n</p><h2><span data-ic=\\\"checkmark\\\" class=\\\"pix-note-ic\\\" contenteditable=\\\"false\\\" style=\\\"color: #f66744\\\"></span>&nbsp;The result</h2><p>\\n\\n</p><p>Dark red, at the end.</p><p>\\n\\n</p><ul><li><b>Save Image Pixaroma (keeps each picture's name)</b> - Saves each picture as JPG into <code>ComfyUI/output/With Logo</code>, named like its picture with <code>_logo</code> at the end.</li></ul><p>\\n\\n</p><hr class=\\\"pix-note-hr-solid\\\" style=\\\"color: #b8b8b8\\\"><p>\\n\\n</p><h2><span data-ic=\\\"info\\\" class=\\\"pix-note-ic\\\" contenteditable=\\\"false\\\" style=\\\"color: #f66744\\\"></span>&nbsp;Readouts</h2><p>\\n\\n</p><p>Dark. Nothing to set: they show you what happened.</p><p>\\n\\n</p><ul><li><b>Run Timer</b> - The dark clock above the result shows how long the last Run took.</li></ul><p>\\n\\n</p>\",\"buttonColor\":\"#f66744\",\"lineColor\":\"#f66744\",\"backgroundColor\":\"#2a2a2a\",\"info\":{\"title\":\"Nodes Info\",\"icon\":\"node-v5\",\"color\":\"#3d7cc9\"}}"
      },
